o knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).</li><li>Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so. The email&#39;s button is <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>: one press makes their Sales application from the one they sent (no new form) and sends the AI interview link at once.</li><li>Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.</li><li>A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.</li><li>Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-review-the-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review the applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Applications.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite anyway</b> sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview days</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Interview days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. A short form opens: the <b class="gd-ui">Role</b> (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the <b class="gd-ui">Start date</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, filled in with the role&#39;s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm: hire and start onboarding</b>. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do&#39;s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email (release 44: no start date in it; training and claiming shifts only, then a hello in the team chat and the member tag &quot;Name - Position&quot; in each WhatsApp group, also a first-day To do); their call slot and AI interview link close.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire&#39;s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line and the answer&#39;s score out of 10. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The interview decides by itself (release 41, on by default again since release 44): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b> on any candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b> holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and <b class="gd-ui">Decide by hand</b> if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-redo-the-ai-interview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Redo the AI interview</h2><p class="gd-p">If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant&#39;s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Redo the AI interview</b>, then confirm.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Their staff access ends if they were already hired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The application goes back to <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b> and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-in-person-needs-the-toronto-area-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list and the candidate page show <b class="gd-ui">Lives in</b>, flag <b class="gd-ui">Location mismatch</b> when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer <b class="gd-ui">Move to Remote Sales</b> to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-dates-before-the-townhall-release-35-widened-in-re" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> here and on the Fleet home page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-call-reminders-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview call reminders (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day&#39;s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> for a phone call). <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Interviews today</b>: each call&#39;s time, candidate, role and its <b class="gd-ui">Join</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-the-sales-funnel-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Sales funnel (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Pipeline tab opens with <b class="gd-ui">Sales funnel</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sales staff in the academy</b>: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows &quot;Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago&quot;. A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The re-send</b>: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The bar for Sales</b>: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI&#39;s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'start-here', 'start', null, '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars staff in Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales, in the office, remote or in person. Everyone works in one staff portal: its menu shows a group for each function you hold. Read chapter 1, then the chapter for each of your functions. If you also do field work (handovers, returns, moving cars), read the Field Guide too: your jobs are under **Field work** in the same menu.

### What you need

- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A computer for your shift. The portal also works on a phone
- An authenticator app on your phone, if your Admin turns on two-step sign-in

## Once you are hired

You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.

1. Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once the academy and your agreement are done).
2. In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as "Name - Position", for example "Maria - Sales", so everyone knows who you are and what you do.

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land in your portal, on **To do**, working as your main function.
3. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission. Change it later under **Profile**, at the top of the menu.
4. Then on **Profile**, **Pay details**: choose how you are paid (bank account, GCash, PayPal, Wise, e-Transfer or through OnlineJobs.ph) and press **Save my pay details**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown; an Admin confirms new details with you.
5. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password, then **Sign in**.
6. Link expired? Press **Send me a new link** on the page it opens, or ask an Admin for a password link.
7. Sign in with your phone: on **Profile**, press **Add and verify my phone number** and enter the 6-digit code we text you. Then press **Use my phone number instead** on the sign-in page. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

![](/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg "phone; size: 390 645; pins: 3 95.4 78.4")

> Good to know: Recommended: open your profile and press **Set up two-step sign-in**. Scan the code with your authenticator app, type the 6 digits and press **Continue**. After that every sign-in asks for a code.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the chapter for that page beside it (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## Work chats only

All work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. Questions, handovers, problems and customer details go in the group, so the whole team sees them and nothing is lost when someone is away. If a colleague or an Admin writes to you privately about work, answer in the group.
', 'Start here', 'Who this is for and your first sign-in.',
  '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars staff in Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales, in the office, remote or in person. Everyone works in one staff portal: its menu shows a group for each function you hold. Read chapter 1, then the chapter for each of your functions. If you also do field work (handovers, returns, moving cars), read the Field Guide too: your jobs are under **Field work** in the same menu.

### What you need

- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A computer for your shift. The portal also works on a phone
- An authenticator app on your phone, if your Admin turns on two-step sign-in

## Once you are hired

You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.

1. Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once your agreement is signed and the academy is passed).
2. In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as "Name - Position", for example "Maria - Sales", so everyone knows who you are and what you do.

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land in your portal, on **To do**, working as your main function.
3. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission. Change it later under **Profile**, at the top of the menu.
4. Then on **Profile**, **Pay details**: choose how you are paid (bank account, GCash, PayPal, Wise, e-Transfer or through OnlineJobs.ph) and press **Save my pay details**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown; an Admin confirms new details with you.
5. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password, then **Sign in**.
6. Link expired? Press **Send me a new link** on the page it opens, or ask an Admin for a password link.
7. Sign in with your phone: on **Profile**, press **Add and verify my phone number** and enter the 6-digit code we text you. Then press **Use my phone number instead** on the sign-in page. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

![](/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg "phone; size: 390 645; pins: 3 95.4 78.4")

> Good to know: Recommended: open your profile and press **Set up two-step sign-in**. Scan the code with your authenticator app, type the 6 digits and press **Continue**. After that every sign-in asks for a code.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the chapter for that page beside it (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## Work chats only

All work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. Questions, handovers, problems and customer details go in the group, so the whole team sees them and nothing is lost when someone is away. If a colleague or an Admin writes to you privately about work, answer in the group.

## Something to check on your record (release 48)

When something on your record looks wrong, a box opens on any page of the portal and says exactly what, with the box to fix it right there: your staff agreement waiting for your driver''s licence number or home address, a home address outside Ontario while you work in person in Toronto (fix it, or press It''s correct and say why), a licence that expires within 30 days (or has expired), pay details missing, a phone number that is not valid, or your WhatsApp member tag not confirmed. Press **Save** and the box checks again.

1. Your agreement waiting for something you give cannot be put off: once you save it, the agreement is made and appears under Documents to sign at once. The sign page says the same when nothing is ready to sign yet.
2. Anything else you can put off with **Remind me later**: it comes back after a day.',
